  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-label">Brent-to-Retail Correlation</div>
    <div class="kpi-value">{corr_petrol}</div>
    <div class="kpi-note">Petrol | Diesel: {corr_diesel}</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-label">Subsidy Dampening Effect</div>
    <div class="kpi-value">{subsidy_dampening}%</div>
    <div class="kpi-note">High-subsidy vs. low-subsidy price gap</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-label">Regional Price Spread</div>
    <div class="kpi-value">${round(yearly_spread.mean(), 2)}/L</div>
    <div class="kpi-note">Avg. spread between highest & lowest region</div>
  </div>
  <div class="kpi-card">
    <div class="kpi-label">Tax Burden by Income</div>
    <div class="kpi-value">{round(tax_kpi.get('High', 0), 1)}% / {round(tax_kpi.get('Middle', 0), 1)}% / {round(tax_kpi.get('Low', 0), 1)}%</div>
    <div class="kpi-note">High / Middle / Low income avg. tax %</div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- TOC -->
<div class="toc">
  <h2>Table of Contents</h2>
  <ol>
    <li><a href="#global-overview">Global Fuel Price Overview</a></li>
    <li><a href="#temporal-trends">Temporal Price Trends & Volatility</a></li>
    <li><a href="#regional-comparison">Regional Price Disparities</a></li>
    <li><a href="#subsidy-tax">Impact of Subsidies and Taxation on Retail Prices</a></li>
    <li><a href="#income-level">Fuel Affordability by Income Level</a></li>
    <li><a href="#key-findings">Key Findings & Policy Implications</a></li>
  </ol>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 1: GLOBAL OVERVIEW -->
<div class="section" id="global-overview">
  <h2><span class="section-num">01</span>Global Fuel Price Overview</h2>

  <p>This section presents summary statistics for the three retail fuel types and the Brent Crude benchmark across the full study period (January 2020 – April 2026), spanning {total_countries} countries and {total_weeks} weekly observations.</p>

  <h3>Summary Statistics</h3>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Fuel Type</th><th>Mean (USD/L)</th><th>Median (USD/L)</th><th>Min (USD/L)</th><th>Max (USD/L)</th><th>Std Dev</th></tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Petrol</strong></td>
      <td>${overall_stats['Petrol']['mean']}</td>
      <td>${overall_stats['Petrol']['median']}</td>
      <td>${overall_stats['Petrol']['min']}</td>
      <td>${overall_stats['Petrol']['max']}</td>
      <td>${overall_stats['Petrol']['std']}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Diesel</strong></td>
      <td>${overall_stats['Diesel']['mean']}</td>
      <td>${overall_stats['Diesel']['median']}</td>
      <td>${overall_stats['Diesel']['min']}</td>
      <td>${overall_stats['Diesel']['max']}</td>
      <td>${overall_stats['Diesel']['std']}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>LPG</strong></td>
      <td>${overall_stats['Lpg']['mean']}</td>
      <td>${overall_stats['Lpg']['median']}</td>
      <td>${overall_stats['Lpg']['min']}</td>
      <td>${overall_stats['Lpg']['max']}</td>
      <td>${overall_stats['Lpg']['std']}</td>
    </tr>
    <tr>
      <td><strong>Brent Crude (USD/bbl)</strong></td>
      <td>${brent_stats['mean']}</td>
      <td>${brent_stats['median']}</td>
      <td>${brent_stats['min']}</td>
      <td>${brent_stats['max']}</td>
      <td>${brent_stats['std']}</td>
    </tr>
  </table>

  <h3>Brent Crude Benchmark</h3>
  <div class="stat-grid">
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-label">Peak Price</div>
      <div class="stat-value">${brent_peak_price}</div>
      <div class="stat-label">{brent_peak_date}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-label">Trough Price</div>
      <div class="stat-value">${brent_trough_price}</div>
      <div class="stat-label">{brent_trough_date}</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-label">Full-Period Range</div>
      <div class="stat-value">${round(brent_stats['max'] - brent_stats['min'], 2)}</div>
      <div class="stat-label">Max – Min spread</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-label">Period Average</div>
      <div class="stat-value">${brent_stats['mean']}</div>
      <div class="stat-label">USD per barrel</div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>Highest & Lowest Petrol Price Countries (Period Average)</h3>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Rank</th><th>Country</th><th>Region</th><th>Income Level</th><th>Subsidy</th><th>Avg Petrol (USD/L)</th></tr>
    {''.join(f'<tr><td>{i+1}</td><td>{r["country"]}</td><td>{r["region"]}</td><td>{r["income_level"]}</td><td><span class="badge {"badge-low" if r["subsidy_level"]=="Low" else "badge-high"}">{r["subsidy_level"]}</span></td><td>${r["petrol_mean"]}</td></tr>' for i, r in top5.iterrows())}
    <tr><td colspan="6" style="text-align:center; color:var(--text-muted); font-style:italic;">…</td></tr>
    {''.join(f'<tr><td>{total_countries - 4 + idx}</td><td>{r["country"]}</td><td>{r["region"]}</td><td>{r["income_level"]}</td><td><span class="badge {"badge-low" if r["subsidy_level"]=="Low" else "badge-high"}">{r["subsidy_level"]}</span></td><td>${r["petrol_mean"]}</td></tr>' for idx, (_, r) in enumerate(bottom5.iterrows()))}
  </table>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 2: TEMPORAL TRENDS -->
<div class="section" id="temporal-trends">
  <h2><span class="section-num">02</span>Temporal Price Trends & Volatility</h2>

  <p>This section tracks the evolution of retail fuel prices and Brent Crude over the study period, with particular focus on the two defining disruptions: the COVID-19 demand collapse (2020) and the 2022 energy price crisis.</p>

  <h3>Weekly Brent Crude & Global Average Retail Prices</h3>
  <div class="chart-container">
    <canvas id="chartTimeline" height="110"></canvas>
    <div class="chart-caption">Weekly Brent Crude (USD/bbl, left axis) vs. global average retail petrol & diesel (USD/L, right axis), January 2020 – April 2026</div>
  </div>

  <h3>Yearly Average Prices</h3>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Year</th><th>Petrol (USD/L)</th><th>Diesel (USD/L)</th><th>Brent (USD/bbl)</th><th>Petrol CV (%)</th><th>Diesel CV (%)</th><th>Brent CV (%)</th></tr>
    {''.join(f'<tr><td>{int(r["year"])}</td><td>${r["petrol_mean"]}</td><td>${r["diesel_mean"]}</td><td>${r["brent_mean"]}</td><td>{r["petrol_std"]}</td><td>{r["diesel_std"]}</td><td>{float(yearly_vol[yearly_vol["year"]==r["year"]]["brent_cv"].values[0])}%</td></tr>' for _, r in yearly.iterrows())}
  </table>

  <h3>Volatility: Coefficient of Variation by Year</h3>
  <div class="chart-container">
    <canvas id="chartVolatility" height="90"></canvas>
    <div class="chart-caption">Coefficient of variation (CV%) for petrol retail prices and Brent Crude by year — higher values indicate greater relative volatility</div>
  </div>

  <h3>COVID-19 Demand Shock (Q1 → Q2 2020)</h3>
  <div class="stat-grid">
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-label">Brent Crude Drop</div>
      <div class="stat-value" style="color:var(--danger)">{covid_drop_brent}%</div>
      <div class="stat-label">Q1 → Q2 2020</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-label">Retail Petrol Drop</div>
      <div class="stat-value" style="color:var(--danger)">{covid_drop_petrol}%</div>
      <div class="stat-label">Q1 → Q2 2020</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-label">Pass-Through Ratio</div>
      <div class="stat-value">{round(abs(covid_drop_petrol / covid_drop_brent), 2)}</div>
      <div class="stat-label">Retail drop / Brent drop</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>The Brent Crude benchmark fell {abs(covid_drop_brent)}% from Q1 to Q2 2020, while retail petrol prices declined {abs(covid_drop_petrol)}% — a pass-through ratio of {round(abs(covid_drop_petrol / covid_drop_brent), 2)}, indicating significant but incomplete transmission of the crude price shock to consumers. Subsidy regimes, fixed taxes, and contracting margins all contributed to the dampened retail response.</p>

  <h3>2022 Energy Crisis (H1 2021 → H1 2022)</h3>
  <div class="stat-grid">
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-label">Brent Crude Surge</div>
      <div class="stat-value" style="color:var(--danger)">+{crisis_rise_brent}%</div>
      <div class="stat-label">H1 2021 → H1 2022</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-label">Retail Petrol Surge</div>
      <div class="stat-value" style="color:var(--danger)">+{crisis_rise_petrol}%</div>
      <div class="stat-label">H1 2021 → H1 2022</div>
    </div>
    <div class="stat-box">
      <div class="stat-label">Pass-Through Ratio</div>
      <div class="stat-value">{round(crisis_rise_petrol / crisis_rise_brent, 2)}</div>
      <div class="stat-label">Retail rise / Brent rise</div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <p>The 2022 energy crisis saw Brent Crude surge {crisis_rise_brent}% from H1 2021 to H1 2022, while retail petrol prices rose {crisis_rise_petrol}%. The pass-through ratio of {round(crisis_rise_petrol / crisis_rise_brent, 2)} suggests that upward crude movements were transmitted to consumers more completely than the downward shock during COVID, consistent with asymmetric "rockets and feathers" pricing dynamics.</p>

  <h3>Brent-to-Retail Price Correlation</h3>
  <table>
    <tr><th>Fuel Type</th><th>Pearson Correlation (r)</th><th>Interpretation</th></tr>
    <tr><td>Petrol</td><td><strong>{corr_petrol}</strong></td><td>{'Strong' if abs(corr_petrol) > 0.7 else 'Moderate'} positive correlation</td></tr>
    <tr><td>Diesel</td><td><strong>{corr_diesel}</strong></td><td>{'Strong' if abs(corr_diesel) > 0.7 else 'Moderate'} positive correlation</td></tr>
    <tr><td>LPG</td><td><strong>{corr_lpg}</strong></td><td>{'Strong' if abs(corr_lpg) > 0.7 else 'Moderate'} positive correlation</td></tr>
  </table>
  <p>The correlation analysis confirms that Brent Crude is a strong driver of retail fuel prices globally. The petrol correlation of {corr_petrol} indicates that Brent movements explain approximately {round(corr_petrol**2 * 100, 1)}% of the variance in weekly global average retail petrol prices.</p>
</div>

<!-- SECTION 3: REGIONAL COMPARISON -->
<div class="section" id="regional-comparison">
  <h2><span class="section-num">03</span>Regional Price Disparities</h2>

  <p>Regional analysis reveals persistent disparities in retail fuel prices, driven by differences in taxation, subsidy regimes, refining capacity, and distribution costs.</p>

  <h3>Average Fuel Prices by Region (Full Period)</h3>
  <div class="chart-container">
    <canvas id="chartRegional" height="100"></canvas>
    <div class="chart-caption">Average retail petrol and diesel prices (USD/L) by geographic region, January 2020 – April 2026</div>
  </div>

  <table>
    <tr><th>Region</th><th>Countries</th><th>Avg Petrol (USD/L)</th><th>Avg Diesel (USD/L)</th><th>Avg LPG (USD/L)</th></tr>
    {''.join(f'<tr><td>{r["region"]}</td><td>{int(r["country_count"])}</td><td>${r["petrol_mean"]}</td><td>${r["diesel_mean"]}</td><td>${r["lpg_mean"]}</td></tr>' for _, r in region_avg.iterrows())}
  </table>

  <p>The <strong>{highest_region}</strong> region registers the highest average petrol price at ${highest_petrol}/L, while <strong>{lowest_region}</strong> has the lowest at ${lowest_petrol}/L — a gap of ${round(highest_petrol - lowest_petrol, 3)}/L.</p>

  <h3>Regional Price Evolution by Year</h3>
  <div class="chart-container">
    <canvas id="chartRegionalYearly" height="110"></canvas>
    <div class="chart-caption">Average retail petrol price (USD/L) by region, 2020–2026 — shows convergence/divergence over time</div>
  </div>

  <h3>Regional Price Spread Over Time</h3>
  <div class="chart-container">
